WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.624
Hi friends!

00:00:00.624 --> 00:00:03.290
Today we're going to learn how to read a clock.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.821
It's easier than you think!

00:00:05.421 --> 00:00:08.458
A clock has the numbers one to twelve, all the

00:00:08.458 --> 00:00:09.977
way around in a circle.

00:00:09.977 --> 00:00:11.693
Twelve is at the very top.

00:00:12.293 --> 00:00:13.691
A clock has two hands.

00:00:13.691 --> 00:00:15.723
The short hand is the hour hand.

00:00:15.723 --> 00:00:17.819
The long hand is the minute hand.

00:00:18.419 --> 00:00:21.251
When the long minute hand points straight up at the

00:00:21.251 --> 00:00:22.972
twelve, it's something o'clock!

00:00:22.972 --> 00:00:25.971
The short hand points at seven, so it's seven o'clock.

00:00:26.571 --> 00:00:28.893
The minute hand counts by fives!

00:00:28.893 --> 00:00:31.506
Each number means five more minutes.

00:00:31.506 --> 00:00:39.200
Five, ten, fifteen, twenty, twenty-five, thirty, thirty-five, forty, forty-five, fifty, fifty-five, sixty!

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.428
When the minute hand points down at the six, it's half past.

00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:44.759
That's thirty minutes.

00:00:44.759 --> 00:00:47.480
This clock says half past two, or two thirty.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.447
When the minute hand points at the three, it's quarter past.

00:00:51.447 --> 00:00:52.738
That's fifteen minutes.

00:00:52.738 --> 00:00:54.309
Here it's quarter past four.

00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:58.280
When the minute hand points at the nine, it's quarter to.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.000
Only fifteen minutes left until the next hour!

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.419
This is quarter to five.

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:03.612
Your turn!

00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:04.679
Look at the clock.

00:01:04.679 --> 00:01:05.628
What time is it?

00:01:05.628 --> 00:01:06.517
Think about it.

00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:11.127
It's eight o'clock!

00:01:11.127 --> 00:01:13.754
The long hand is on the twelve, and the short

00:01:13.754 --> 00:01:14.980
hand is on the eight.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:15.564
Great job!

00:01:16.164 --> 00:01:17.344
Here's another one.

00:01:17.344 --> 00:01:19.331
Where is the long hand pointing?

00:01:19.331 --> 00:01:20.324
What time is it?

00:01:23.824 --> 00:01:25.028
It's half past six!

00:01:25.028 --> 00:01:27.690
The long hand is on the six, and the short

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.591
hand is between six and seven.

00:01:29.591 --> 00:01:30.288
You did it!

00:01:30.888 --> 00:01:34.163
Now you know the hour hand, the minute hand, o'clock,

00:01:34.163 --> 00:01:36.821
half past, and quarter past and quarter to.

00:01:36.821 --> 00:01:38.675
Keep practicing, clock reader!
